<BaseLayout title="About | KJH Dev" description="About KJH Dev and the practical software development experience behind this blog." lang="en" koUrl="/ko/about/" enUrl="/en/about/">
  <article class="post-content">
    <h1>About KJH Dev</h1>
    <p>KJH Dev documents problems and solutions encountered while building and operating software.</p>
    <h2>Topics</h2>
    <p>The blog focuses on practical backend development with Spring Boot and Node.js, MySQL, Docker and Linux server operations, Flutter applications, GitHub Actions, deployment, and related development workflows.</p>
    <h2>How articles are written</h2>
    <p>The goal is to go beyond feature summaries. Articles prioritize the environment in which a problem occurred, how the cause was narrowed down, what was changed, and how the result was verified. Commands and configuration examples include context so they can be adapted rather than copied blindly.</p>
    <p>Software behavior can change between versions, so readers should also check the publication date and environment described in each article.</p>
    <h2>Purpose</h2>
    <p>The site is intended to turn real development work into reusable technical notes and to help other developers shorten the time needed to solve similar problems.</p>
    <h2>Projects and practical technical notes</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/en/projects/stock-market-daily-briefing/">Stock Market Daily Briefing System</a> series follows data collection design, preflight validation, and automated delivery. The <a href="/en/notes/">development notes</a> focus on troubleshooting conditions and verification steps from software operations.</p>
    <p>Examples include <a href="/en/posts/apache-node-reverse-proxy/">debugging Apache reverse proxy and Node.js 404 errors</a> and <a href="/en/posts/mysql-nextval-concurrency/">avoiding MySQL sequence allocation races</a>. The goal is to make each explanation useful in a specific environment rather than presenting commands without context.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>